.TH KRGB 1 "2026-07-11" "k-rgb 0.3.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
krgb \- control RGB lighting on Alienware AW410K/AW510K keyboards
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B krgb
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B krgb
is a Qt6/KDE graphical application that controls the per-key RGB lighting
of Alienware AW410K and AW510K keyboards on Linux.
.PP
It talks directly to the keyboard over hidraw, requires no vendor software,
and provides profiles, hardware effects, a per-key colour editor, and a
system-tray quick switcher.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Display help and exit.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Display version information and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-tray
Start hidden in the system tray.
.TP
.B \-\-apply
Apply the current profile and then exit (useful for autostart).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $HOME/.config/krgbrc
User settings and profiles.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/udev/rules.d/60-alienware-rgb.rules
Udev rule granting the logged-in desktop user access to the keyboard.
.SH AUTHOR
Randy Yates <randyyates@gmail.com>
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR krgb-cli (1)
